{{Otheruses|Tatoo}}
{{Quote|Profiling tattoo markings for criminal activity is troublesome, as it can be a legitimate cultural artifact for some species, and wearing such markings is not criminal.|Police officer [[Exantor Divo]]|<ref name="Scum">''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]''</ref>}}
[[File:YarzionTattoosKelnacca-Kelnacca1.png|thumb|right|210px|[[Jedi Master]] [[Kelnacca]] has [[Yarzion Vell|Vell's]] name tattooed on his head.]]
'''Tattoos''' were markings that covered parts of certain [[Sentience|sentient]] lifeforms' bodies.

For some [[species]], tattoos were part of their culture.<ref name="Scum" /> For example, [[Gender|male]] [[Dathomirian]]s, the [[Nightbrothers]], such as the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth]] [[Maul]], had natural striping that they embellished with tattoos. Female Dathomirians, the [[Nightsisters]], had more subtle tattoos that were in contrast to their pale skin.<ref name="Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

The [[Jedi]] [[Jedi hunter|hunter]] known as [[the Grand Inquisitor]] had [[Color|red]] tattoos on his face.<ref name="Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref>

Some criminal gangs branded their heritage and affiliation through tattoos. Usually, the more elaborate a person's markings were, the more deeply entrenched and storied were their history with the gang.<ref name="Scum" />

[[File:Devaronian_prisoner_SaV.png|thumb|left|210px|A [[Devaronian]] [[prisoner]] with facial tattoos]]
It was possible to give someone temporary tattoos using color sticks. The [[Mandalorian]] [[artist]] [[Sabine Wren]] would decorate her arm using this method, experimenting with different designs.<ref name="Rebel Sketchbook">''[[Sabine My Rebel Sketchbook]]''</ref>

There were also electro-conductive pigment patterns that could hold data and could be used to smuggle confiscated information,<ref name="Scum" /> resulting in so-called ''[[electro-tattoo]]s''. [[Naley Frifa]], an [[outlaw tech]] on [[Vandor]], was also a tattoo [[artist]] who was proficient in [[ink]]ing such electro-tattoos, as well as more mundane tattoos like gang symbols. Frifa herself had numerous tattoos, including a stylized depiction of a [[hyperspace]] [[simu-tunnel]] on her neck and upper torso, and one on her left [[Limb|arm]] of the word "Hiro."<ref name="SoloOG">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref> The human [[Chelli Lona Aphra]] also had electro-tattoos.<ref name="Aphra 14">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 14|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 14]]</ref>

Tattoo recognition could be used for security purposes. Certain tattoo patterns could be spotted by automatic sensors and seasoned [[Law enforcement agency|police officers]]. The [[Imperial Office of Criminal Investigations]] had troves of records of tattoo symbology, and the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] utilized [[protocol droid]]s that specialized in tattoo recognition, using them in transit areas and crowded [[spaceport]]s.<ref name="Scum" />
